{"path":"cargo/guide/project-layout.html","title":"Package Layout","description":"Cargo uses conventions for file placement to make it easy to dive into a new Cargo package:","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":"package-layout","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package Layout"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cargo uses conventions for file placement to make it easy to dive into a new Cargo "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#package","title":"\"package\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"text","value":"package"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"text","code":".\n├── Cargo.lock\n├── Cargo.toml\n├── src/\n│   ├── lib.rs\n│   ├── main.rs\n│   └── bin/\n│       ├── named-executable.rs\n│       ├── another-executable.rs\n│       └── multi-file-executable/\n│           ├── main.rs\n│           └── some_module.rs\n├── benches/\n│   ├── large-input.rs\n│   └── multi-file-bench/\n│       ├── main.rs\n│       └── bench_module.rs\n├── examples/\n│   ├── simple.rs\n│   └── multi-file-example/\n│       ├── main.rs\n│       └── ex_module.rs\n└── tests/\n    ├── some-integration-tests.rs\n    └── multi-file-test/\n        ├── main.rs\n        └── test_module.rs"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.lock"},{"type":"text","value":" are stored in the root of your package ("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"package root"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source code goes in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"src"},{"type":"text","value":" directory."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default library file is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"src/lib.rs"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default executable file is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"src/main.rs"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other executables can be placed in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"src/bin/"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Benchmarks go in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"benches"},{"type":"text","value":" directory."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples go in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"examples"},{"type":"text","value":" directory."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Integration tests go in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"tests"},{"type":"text","value":" directory."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a binary, example, bench, or integration test consists of multiple source files, place a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"main.rs"},{"type":"text","value":" file along with the extra "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#module","title":"\"module\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"modules"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" within a subdirectory of the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"src/bin"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"examples"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"benches"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"tests"},{"type":"text","value":" directory. The name of the executable will be the directory name."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" By convention, binaries, examples, benches and integration tests follow "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"kebab-case"},{"type":"text","value":" naming style, unless there are compatibility reasons to do otherwise (e.g. compatibility with a pre-existing binary name). Modules within those targets are "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"snake_case"},{"type":"text","value":" following the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/0430-finalizing-naming-conventions.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rust standard"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can learn more about Rust’s module system in "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch07-00-managing-growing-projects-with-packages-crates-and-modules.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"the book"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/cargo-targets.html#configuring-a-target","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuring a target"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more details on manually configuring targets. See "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/cargo-targets.html#target-auto-discovery","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Target auto-discovery"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more information on controlling how Cargo automatically infers target names."}]}]}}
